  "_comment": "Shared TS/Python fixture for obligations. Each case is a stubbed engine `details` payload and either the exact obligations the SDK must derive from it, in wire spelling (redact / max_items / log_values / extra as {name: [sorted values]}), or `error: true` when derivation must fail closed (TS AuthorizeError / Python AuthorizeError, fixed message). `expected` is serialised by both lanes with sorted keys and compared byte-for-byte; `redact` is listed sorted because the merge is a set union. The verdict gate (only an Allow carries obligations) is exercised separately by each lane with `stub_decisions`.",
